        "original_id": "e78ed95b-667c-53dd-8171-274d48f9dc86",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Keenan, Leofric\n- Works: The Exeter Book, Codex Exoniensis\n- Organizations: Exeter Cathedral, Exeter Cathedral Library\n- Roles: bishop of Exeter\n- Concepts: Anglo-Saxon texts, Anglo-Saxon poetry, the natural world\n\nFacts:\n- The Exeter Book, also known as the Codex Exoniensis and Exeter Cathedral Library MS 3501, is a tenth-century codex that anthologizes Anglo-Saxon poetry.\n- In 1072, Leofric, the first bishop of Exeter, donated the Exeter Book to the library of Exeter Cathedral.\n- Paul Keenan's body of composition spans 27 years.\n- Paul Keenan's compositions consistently explore Anglo-Saxon texts from The Exeter Book and the natural world.",
